{"name":"Snowed In","hex":"#e8e5de","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snowed in","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Unable to exit a place or location due to excessive snow."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of snow in"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowed_in"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snowed In","blocks":[{"text":"Snowed In is the first Christmas album by American pop rock group Hanson. It was quickly released following the success of their previous album, Middle of Nowhere, and was recorded in London. Snowed In was also the best-selling holiday album for 1997 in the United States, selling 863,000 copies that year according to Nielsen SoundScan. It has since sold a total of 1,081,000 copies in the US."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/87/Hanson-Snowed_In.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowed_In"},{"title":"Snowed In (serial)","blocks":[{"text":"Snowed In is a 1926 American silent drama film serial in 10 episodes/chapters. Directed by Spencer Gordon Bennet, the film stars Allene Ray and Walter Miller. Aviation film historian James H. Farmer considered Snowed In as an \"above average serial of the period.\""}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Snowed_In_lobby_card_2.jpg/330px-Snowed_In_lobby_card_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snowed_In_(serial)"},{"title":"Snow","blocks":[{"text":"Snow is a form of solid atmospheric precipitation consisting of individual ice crystals that grow while suspended in the air—usually within clouds—and then fall, accumulating on the ground, where they undergo further changes. It consists of frozen crystalline water throughout its life cycle, starting when, under suitable conditions, the ice crystals form in the atmosphere, increase to millimeter size, precipitate and accumulate on surfaces, then metamorphose in place, and ultimately melt, slide, or sublimate away."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg/330px-CargoNet_Di_12_Euro_4000_L%C3%B8nsdal_-_Bolna.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Snowed_In_ad_in_Motion_Picture_News%2C_July_10%2C_1926.png/500px-Snowed_In_ad_in_Motion_Picture_News%2C_July_10%2C_1926.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Snowed_In_ad_in_Motion_Picture_News%2C_July_10%2C_1926.png/1280px-Snowed_In_ad_in_Motion_Picture_News%2C_July_10%2C_1926.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Snowed_In_ad_in_Motion_Picture_News%2C_July_10%2C_1926.png/500px-Snowed_In_ad_in_Motion_Picture_News%2C_July_10%2C_1926.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Snowed In ad in Motion Picture News, July 10, 1926","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASnowed_In_ad_in_Motion_Picture_News%2C_July_10%2C_1926.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/500px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/1280px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Feb242007_blizzard.gif/500px-Feb242007_blizzard.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Extratropical cyclonic snowstorm, February 24, 2007